IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch5`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 5A: pension increase or lump sum where entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred.
-- The converter dropped the paragraph numbers; paragraphs 1 to 5 follow the in-text citations ("paragraph 2 (entitlement to increase of
-- pension)", "paragraph 4 (entitlement to lump sum)", "paragraph 3", "paragraph 5", "paragraph 1(1)(a)"). NOTES.md has the labels.
-- It imports ssc9-sch5 for the 12-month count and the accrual-period rules whose words it repeats.

§ `Schedule 5A -- pension increase or lump sum where entitlement to shared additional pension is deferred`

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- choice between pension increase and lump sum`

DECLARE `sch 5A Election` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5A para 1(1)(a) an election that paragraph 2 (the increase of pension) applies`
    `sch 5A para 1(1)(b) an election that paragraph 4 (the lump sum) applies`

DECLARE `sch 5A Party` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5A the person whose entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred`

DECLARE `sch 5A Act` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5A makes an election` HAS `the choice` IS A `sch 5A Election`

-- 1(1): where the entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred and the deferment is at least 12 months the person shall elect.
-- "Where" is not an "if": outside it the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:5295 | (1) Where a person’s entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred and the period of deferment is at least 12 months, the person shall, on claiming his pension or within a prescribed period after claiming it, elect in the prescribed manner either—
-- src:5296 | (a) that paragraph 2 (entitlement to increase of pension) is to apply in relation to the period of deferment, or
-- src:5297 | (b) that paragraph 4 (entitlement to lump sum) is to apply in relation to the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5A para 1(1) (src:5295-5297)
GIVEN `the entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of deferment` IS A Period
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5A para 1(1) the person must elect` MEANS
    IF NOT `the entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person’s entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred"
    ELSE CONSIDER `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` `the period of deferment`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 29 February fork of the 12 months (F1)
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and the period of deferment is at least 12 months"

-- 1(1) and (2) as a regulative rule: elect on claiming or within the prescribed period after claiming; the lapse is dealt with by 1(2)
-- (treated as a (b) election), so it leads to FULFILLED, not to a breach.
-- src:5295 | (1) Where a person’s entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred and the period of deferment is at least 12 months, the person shall, on claiming his pension or within a prescribed period after claiming it, elect in the prescribed manner either—
-- src:5296 | (a) that paragraph 2 (entitlement to increase of pension) is to apply in relation to the period of deferment, or
-- src:5297 | (b) that paragraph 4 (entitlement to lump sum) is to apply in relation to the period of deferment.
-- src:5298 | (2) If no election under sub-paragraph (1) is made within the period prescribed under that sub-paragraph, the person is to be treated as having made an election under sub-paragraph (1)(b).
@ref sch 5A para 1(1) and (2) (src:5295-5298)
GIVEN `the prescribed period after claiming, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 5A Party` `sch 5A Act`
`sch 5A para 1(1) the election duty` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 5A the person whose entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred`
    MUST `sch 5A makes an election` choice
    WITHIN `the prescribed period after claiming, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

-- src:5298 | (2) If no election under sub-paragraph (1) is made within the period prescribed under that sub-paragraph, the person is to be treated as having made an election under sub-paragraph (1)(b).
@ref sch 5A para 1(2) (src:5298)
GIVEN `the election made within the prescribed period` IS A MAYBE `sch 5A Election`
GIVETH A `sch 5A Election`
`sch 5A para 1(2) the election that is treated as made` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the election made within the prescribed period`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `sch 5A para 1(1)(b) an election that paragraph 4 (the lump sum) applies`
    WHEN JUST chosen THEN chosen

-- 1(3): regulations (change of election; avoiding duplication of payment): a regulation-making power, inert (machinery).

§§ `Paragraph 2 -- increase of pension where entitlement is deferred`

-- 2(1): applies where the entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred and either (a) the deferment is under 12 months or
-- (b) the person made a paragraph 1(1)(a) election. "applies where": otherwise NOTHING.
-- src:5305 | (1) This paragraph applies where a person’s entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred and either—
-- src:5306 | (a) the period of deferment is less than 12 months, or
-- src:5307 | (b) the person has made an election under paragraph 1(1)(a) in relation to the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5A para 2(1) (src:5305-5307)
GIVEN `the entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of deferment` IS A Period
      `the election made, or treated as made` IS A MAYBE `sch 5A Election`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5A para 2(1) this paragraph applies` MEANS
    IF NOT `the entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies where a person’s entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred"
    ELSE CONSIDER `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` `the period of deferment`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 29 February fork of the 12 months (F1)
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE   -- limb (a): "the period of deferment is less than 12 months"
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             CONSIDER `the election made, or treated as made`
             WHEN JUST `sch 5A para 1(1)(a) an election that paragraph 2 (the increase of pension) applies` THEN JUST TRUE   -- limb (b)
             WHEN JUST `sch 5A para 1(1)(b) an election that paragraph 4 (the lump sum) applies` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): neither (a) nor (b) is met
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no election is recorded

-- 2(2): the rate is increased by the aggregate of the increments, but only if that is enough to increase the rate by at least 1 per cent.
-- src:5308 | (2) The rate of the person’s shared additional pension shall be increased by an amount equal to the aggregate of the increments to which he is entitled under paragraph 3, but only if that amount is enough to increase the rate of the pension by at least 1 per cent.
@ref sch 5A para 2(2) (src:5308)
GIVEN `the aggregate of the increments under paragraph 3` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate of the shared additional pension before the increase` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5A para 2(2) the amount by which the rate of the pension is increased` MEANS
    IF `the aggregate of the increments under paragraph 3` AT LEAST (`the weekly rate of the shared additional pension before the increase` DIVIDED BY 100)
    THEN `the aggregate of the increments under paragraph 3`
    ELSE 0   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but only if that amount is enough to increase the rate of the pension by at least 1 per cent"

§§ `Paragraph 3 -- calculation of increment`

-- 3(5): "incremental period" means any period of six days treated by regulations as days of increment (NOTES.md, F3: the reading of six days).
-- src:5314 | (5) In this paragraph “incremental period” means any period of six days which are treated by regulations as days of increment for the purposes of this paragraph in relation to the person and pension in question.
@ref sch 5A para 3(5) (src:5314)
GIVEN `the number of days in the period of deferment that regulations treat as days of increment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5A para 3(5) the number of complete incremental periods` MEANS
    FLOOR (`the number of days in the period of deferment that regulations treat as days of increment` DIVIDED BY 6)

-- 3(1): an increment for each complete incremental period.
-- src:5310 | (1) A person is entitled to an increment under this paragraph for each complete incremental period in his period of deferment.
@ref sch 5A para 3(1) (src:5310)
GIVEN `the number of complete incremental periods` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5A para 3(1) the number of increments` MEANS
    `the number of complete incremental periods`

-- 3(3) and (4): rounding of an amount under 3(2) to the nearest penny, "taking any 1/2p as nearest to the next whole penny"
-- (read as upward: NOTES.md, F6); an amount under 1/2p is zero notwithstanding any other provision.
-- src:5312 | (3) Amounts under sub-paragraph (2) shall be rounded to the nearest penny, taking any 1/2p as nearest to the next whole penny.
-- src:5313 | (4) Where an amount under sub-paragraph (2) would, apart from this sub-paragraph, be a sum less than 1/2p, the amount shall be taken to be zero, notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, the Pensions Act or the Administration Act.
@ref sch 5A para 3(3) and (4) (src:5312-5313)
GIVEN `the amount under sub-paragraph (2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5A para 3(3) the amount under sub-paragraph (2) as rounded` MEANS
    IF `the amount under sub-paragraph (2)` LESS THAN 0.005
    THEN 0   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the amount shall be taken to be zero, notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, the Pensions Act or the Administration Act"
    ELSE (FLOOR ((`the amount under sub-paragraph (2)` TIMES 100) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 100

-- 3(2): the increment for an incremental period is 1/5th per cent of the weekly rate of the shared additional pension to which the person
-- would have been entitled had the entitlement not been deferred, rounded by 3(3) and (4).
-- src:5311 | (2) The amount of the increment for an incremental period shall be 1/ 5th per cent. of the weekly rate of the shared additional pension to which the person would have been entitled for the period if his entitlement had not been deferred.
@ref sch 5A para 3(2) (src:5311)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the shared additional pension to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5A para 3(2) the increment for one incremental period` MEANS
    `sch 5A para 3(3) the amount under sub-paragraph (2) as rounded` ((`the weekly rate of the shared additional pension to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred` DIVIDED BY 5) DIVIDED BY 100)

-- The aggregate of the increments (used by 2(2)).
-- src:5310 | (1) A person is entitled to an increment under this paragraph for each complete incremental period in his period of deferment.
-- src:5311 | (2) The amount of the increment for an incremental period shall be 1/ 5th per cent. of the weekly rate of the shared additional pension to which the person would have been entitled for the period if his entitlement had not been deferred.
@ref sch 5A para 3 (src:5310-5311)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the shared additional pension to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days in the period of deferment that regulations treat as days of increment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5A para 3 the aggregate of the increments` MEANS
    (`sch 5A para 3(1) the number of increments` (`sch 5A para 3(5) the number of complete incremental periods` `the number of days in the period of deferment that regulations treat as days of increment`))
    TIMES (`sch 5A para 3(2) the increment for one incremental period` `the weekly rate of the shared additional pension to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred`)

-- 3(6): an order under section 150 that came into force during the deferment is treated as in force from before it began.
-- src:5315 | (6) Where one or more orders have come into force under section 150 of the Administration Act during the period of deferment, the rate for any incremental period shall be determined as if the order or orders had come into force before the beginning of the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5A para 3(6) (src:5315)
GIVEN `an order under section 150 of the Administration Act came into force during the period of deferment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate as it would be had the order or orders come into force before the beginning of the period of deferment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5A para 3(6) the rate for an incremental period` MEANS
    IF `an order under section 150 of the Administration Act came into force during the period of deferment`
    THEN JUST `the weekly rate as it would be had the order or orders come into force before the beginning of the period of deferment`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where one or more orders have come into force under section 150 ... during the period of deferment"

-- 3(7): the sums are subject to alteration by order under section 150: a power exercised outside these sources; inert (machinery).

-- Paragraph 2 as a whole.
-- src:5305 | (1) This paragraph applies where a person’s entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred and either—
-- src:5306 | (a) the period of deferment is less than 12 months, or
-- src:5307 | (b) the person has made an election under paragraph 1(1)(a) in relation to the period of deferment.
-- src:5308 | (2) The rate of the person’s shared additional pension shall be increased by an amount equal to the aggregate of the increments to which he is entitled under paragraph 3, but only if that amount is enough to increase the rate of the pension by at least 1 per cent.
@ref sch 5A para 2 (src:5305-5308)
GIVEN `the entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of deferment` IS A Period
      `the election made, or treated as made` IS A MAYBE `sch 5A Election`
      `the weekly rate of the shared additional pension to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days in the period of deferment that regulations treat as days of increment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5A para 2 the amount by which the shared additional pension is increased for the deferment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 5A para 2(1) this paragraph applies` `the entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred` `the period of deferment` `the election made, or treated as made`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (`sch 5A para 2(2) the amount by which the rate of the pension is increased` aggregate `the weekly rate of the shared additional pension to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred`)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 2(1) never answers FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 2(1) does not apply on these facts
    WHERE
        aggregate MEANS `sch 5A para 3 the aggregate of the increments` `the weekly rate of the shared additional pension to which the person would have been entitled for the period if the entitlement had not been deferred` `the number of days in the period of deferment that regulations treat as days of increment`

§§ `Paragraph 4 -- lump sum where entitlement is deferred`

-- src:5318 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:5319 | (a) a person’s entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred, and
-- src:5320 | (b) the person has made (or is treated as having made) an election under paragraph 1(1)(b) in relation to the period of deferment.
-- src:5321 | (2) The person is entitled to an amount calculated in accordance with paragraph 5 (a “lump sum”).
@ref sch 5A para 4 (src:5318-5321)
GIVEN `the entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the election made, or treated as made` IS A MAYBE `sch 5A Election`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5A para 4(2) the person is entitled to a lump sum` MEANS
    IF `the entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred` AND (`the election made, or treated as made` EQUALS JUST `sch 5A para 1(1)(b) an election that paragraph 4 (the lump sum) applies`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies where (a) ... and (b) ..."

§§ `Paragraph 5 -- calculation of lump sum`

-- 5(2): "accrual period" is as in paragraph 3B(2) of Schedule 5, in the same words.
-- src:5326 | ‘accrual period’ means any period of seven days beginning with a prescribed day of the week, where that day falls within the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5A para 5(2) (src:5326)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` IS A NUMBER
      `the period of deferment` IS A Period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 5A para 5(2) an accrual period begins on the day` MEANS
    `sch 5 para 3B(2) an accrual period begins on the day` day `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` `the period of deferment`

-- 5(1): the lump sum is the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment.
-- src:5323 | (1) The lump sum is the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5A para 5(1) (src:5323)
GIVEN `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` IS A NUMBER
      `the period of deferment` IS A Period
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
`sch 5A para 5(1) the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment` MEANS
    `sch 5 para 3B(1) the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment` `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` `the period of deferment`

-- 5(3): the formula that gives the accrued amount is omitted from this text, as in Schedule 5 paragraph 3B(3).
-- 5(2) defines "accrued amount" as the amount this sub-paragraph calculates, so the definition is cited here.
-- src:5324 | (2) In this paragraph—
-- src:5325 | ‘accrued amount’ means the amount calculated in accordance with sub-paragraph (3);
-- src:5327 | (3) The accrued amount for an accrual period for a person is—
-- src:5328 | where—
-- src:5329 | A is the accrued amount for the previous accrual period (or, in the case of the first accrual period beginning during the period of deferment, zero);
-- src:5330 | P is the amount of the shared additional pension to which the person would have been entitled for the accrual period if his entitlement had not been deferred;
@ref sch 5A para 5(2) accrued amount, para 5(3) (src:5324-5325) (src:5327-5330)
GIVEN `A, the accrued amount for the previous accrual period` IS A NUMBER
      `P, the amount of the shared additional pension for the accrual period` IS A NUMBER
      `R, the percentage rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5A para 5(3) the accrued amount for an accrual period` MEANS
    NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the formula that combines A, P and R is omitted from this text

-- 5(3) R: two per cent higher than the Bank of England base rate or, if a higher rate is prescribed for paragraphs 3B and 7B of
-- Schedule 5, that higher rate.
-- src:5331 | R is—
-- src:5332 | a percentage rate two per cent. higher than the Bank of England base rate, or
-- src:5333 | if a higher rate is prescribed for the purposes of paragraphs 3B and 7B of Schedule 5, that higher rate.
@ref sch 5A para 5(3) R (src:5331-5333)
GIVEN `the Bank of England base rate, in per cent` IS A NUMBER
      `the higher rate prescribed for the purposes of paragraphs 3B and 7B of Schedule 5` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5A para 5(3) the percentage rate R` MEANS
    `sch 5 para 3B(3) the percentage rate R` `the Bank of England base rate, in per cent` `the higher rate prescribed for the purposes of paragraphs 3B and 7B of Schedule 5`

-- 5(4): a change in the base rate takes effect at the beginning of the accrual period immediately following the one in which it took effect.
-- src:5334 | (4) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (3), any change in the Bank of England base rate is to be treated as taking effect—
-- src:5335 | (a) at the beginning of the accrual period immediately following the accrual period during which the change took effect, or
-- src:5336 | (b) if regulations so provide, at such other time as may be prescribed.
@ref sch 5A para 5(4) (src:5334-5336)
GIVEN `the day the change in the base rate took effect` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` IS A NUMBER
      `the other time regulations provide, if they so provide` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 5A para 5(4) the day a change in the base rate is treated as taking effect` MEANS
    `sch 5 para 3B(4) the day a change in the base rate is treated as taking effect` `the day the change in the base rate took effect` `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` `the other time regulations provide, if they so provide`

-- 5(5): the shared additional pension counted for an accrual period does not include, in prescribed circumstances, such amount as is prescribed.
-- src:5337 | (5) For the purpose of the calculation of the lump sum, the amount of the shared additional pension to which the person would have been entitled for an accrual period does not include, in prescribed circumstances, such amount as may be prescribed.
@ref sch 5A para 5(5) (src:5337)
GIVEN `the shared additional pension to which the person would have been entitled for the accrual period` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount prescribed to be left out in prescribed circumstances` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5A para 5(5) the amount of shared additional pension counted for an accrual period` MEANS
    `the shared additional pension to which the person would have been entitled for the accrual period` MINUS `the amount prescribed to be left out in prescribed circumstances`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not include, in prescribed circumstances, such amount as may be prescribed"

-- 5(6): the lump sum is rounded to the nearest penny, "taking any 1/2p as nearest to the next whole penny" (read as upward: F6).
-- src:5338 | (6) The lump sum must be rounded to the nearest penny, taking any 1/2p as nearest to the next whole penny.
@ref sch 5A para 5(6) (src:5338)
GIVEN `the lump sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5A para 5(6) the lump sum as rounded` MEANS
    (FLOOR ((`the lump sum` TIMES 100) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 100

-- 5(1): the lump sum before rounding is the accrued amount for the last accrual period; the formula is omitted, so the amount is an input.
-- src:5323 | (1) The lump sum is the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment.
@ref sch 5A para 5(1) (src:5323)
GIVEN `the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5A para 5(1) the lump sum before rounding` MEANS
    `the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment`
